{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLVED the plan-review snapshot blocker. Root cause: two EMPTY, untracked directories in .tickets-tracker/ (211c-45bf-3966-4b61, acd3-837b-6e13-40ed) — debris of an interrupted rebar write (~10:05 today), never committed (hence git grep=0). The LOCAL rebar build (HEAD b301e7, 10 commits behind origin/main) has an OLD relation-snapshot reducer that HARD-FAILS (reducer-error) on an event-less ticket dir, blocking review-plan for every ticket whose dependency-closure walk hit it. origin/main (5892134) FIXED this: it skips such a dir with a WARNING ('debris of an interrupted write; safe to delete') instead of erroring — verified by building origin/main in a throwaway worktree and re-running review-plan (reducer passed; only remaining INDETERMINATE cause = missing [agents] LLM extra). Applied the data-side fix too: rmdir'd both empty debris dirs; the OLD local build now also passes the reducer (indet []). Net: the blocker was environmental (stale local debris + a since-fixed reducer), NOT a defect in the authored DC rich-text tickets. Recommendation: update local main to origin/main (carries the tolerant reducer + 9 other fixes incl. 'Normalize reconciler baselines before storage')."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785802092733086001,"uuid":"9bf0f8c6-a0d6-435f-a5b3-491776ed7260"}